# Deterministic isolated race-fixture setup (issue 151)

Base: `6396853ddef7dda305c3daf84d12bb1260eb2a7a`.
Only the race fixture, its controls and this receipt change. Production
drivers, gates, schema, canonical seed and root integration are unchanged.

## Measured mechanism

The selected local D1 double-click case initialized its fresh database with
100 individual driver queries and zero batches. Instrumented setup took
6514.3168 ms; the entire case took 10134 ms. The earlier uninstrumented
single-case run took 5735 ms, illustrating run variance rather than a fixed
baseline. Both selected runs passed and selected out the other 34 cases;
neither was a full-suite run.

The new helper executes the unchanged canonical seed once on a private local
in-memory database and records its actual ordered statements, including the
generated IDs determined by its readbacks. It closes that database and restores
the previous name environment. The immutable statement plan is cached once
per test process; each target receives fresh statement/parameter arrays.
The existing optional PRAGMA stays outside the batch. Schema and seed execute
in one target batch. No database instance or race state is shared or reused.

The same selected case then used one query plus one batch: setup 2095.1063 ms,
whole case 6724 ms. A subsequent bounded two-case D1 slice measured setup
1034.2062 and 838.7195 ms, again one query/one batch each. These are actual
performance.now intervals including fixture compilation when cold and local
workerd IPC; they are not model estimates or hosted-provider measurements.
Compilation caches may be reused. Test answers and target database state are
fresh; only the deterministic statement plan is intentionally reused.

